WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.587
- Many people around the
world are asking themselves,

00:00:02.587 --> 00:00:05.520
"How many doses of the COVID
19 vaccine they'll need

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.353
and how often?"

00:00:06.353 --> 00:00:08.350
- [Narrator] Protection
from vaccines starts waning

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.570
after a few months.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:13.320
So the US and other countries
are expediting booster shots

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.960
to fight rising infections.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.580
- We have booster shots
for the whole nation.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.050
- [Narrator] People in a handful
of places, including Chile

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:23.190
and Israel have even started
getting boosters of boosters.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:24.980
- I'm getting the fourth shot today

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:28.140
'cause I think it's
important for protecting.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.480
- [Narrator] Here in Tel Aviv,

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.880
researchers have been
conducting clinical trials

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.320
for these fourth shots.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:35.380
- The good news is preliminary results

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:38.350
from the Pfizer trial
show a fivefold increase

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.677
in antibodies, researchers hearsay,

00:00:40.677 --> 00:00:42.640
"That could mean increased protection."

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.330
We did not see any severe,
significant adverse events.

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:47.840
- [Narrator] But
scientists are still trying

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.330
to determine just how effective
these fourth doses are,

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:52.560
and how long that protection can last,

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:55.370
and some warn against
rushing to add more boosters.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:58.680
- Regarding a fourth dose,
I'm not convinced at all.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:02.240
I think that's why it shouldn't
be done in a clinical trial.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.180
- [Narrator] So we looked
at what the scientists know

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:05.937
and why many epidemiologists say,

00:01:05.937 --> 00:01:09.185
"Repeated doses shouldn't
be given out so quickly."

00:01:09.185 --> 00:01:10.470
(background chatter)

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.070
Scientists say, "Vaccine
effectiveness starts to decrease

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:16.520
at around six months," and
that's where boosters come in.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.150
In simple terms, this is how it works.

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:22.340
We all have these Y-shaped
molecules called antibodies.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.610
They are produced naturally
by our body's immune system

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:26.610
to help stop the virus from intruding.

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:28.400
When a virus enters our system,

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.460
our body responds in a number of ways.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:33.710
The first offense is by creating
unique antibodies that bind

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:36.310
to it in order to
neutralize it or remove it.

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:39.640
The COVID-19 vaccine helps the
body to make these antibodies

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.990
and evolve any existing ones,
and to keep the virus out.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.070
But after a while, numbers can dwindle

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:47.150
and that protection fades.

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:50.120
Booster doses increased the
number of antibodies again,

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.220
and continue to advance
the body's understanding

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:53.190
of the virus.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:54.380
(background chatter)

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.890
Now, researchers in Israel

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:57.760
where COVID vaccination started earlier

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.970
than in other countries,
say, "The protection

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:02.330
from those boosters is waning too.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:04.770
In as little as three
months in some cases."

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.290
Professor Gili Regev-Yochay
and her team are working

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:10.121
to determine how effective
a fourth dose will be

00:02:10.121 --> 00:02:12.990
in renewing immunity loss
after the third shot.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.250
- People here that came

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:18.620
to this study are only four
months after the third dose.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:20.860
- [Narrator] The doses are
being tested on staff members

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:23.650
who received a third
Pfizer shot in August.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:25.980
Shira Galper is a
physician at the hospital.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:30.460
- I didn't have any large
concerns participating

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:31.310
in the trial.

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:34.010
I think I would take
vaccine every six months

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.860
if that's what medically is recommended.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:39.730
- [Narrator] The trial has
around 300 participants in total,

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:41.920
half are receiving another Pfizer shot

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:43.780
while the rest are getting Moderna.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:47.690
- The logic behind this is that we think

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:51.530
that there may be a benefit
of combining vaccines.

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:54.621
We're hopeful that we will
see something additive

00:02:54.621 --> 00:02:58.330
when we give or boost the immune response

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.360
with something slightly different.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.360
- [Narrator] The shots
participants got were the same

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:05.060
as are used in normal vaccination cycles,

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:07.560
Pfizer, Moderna, and Johnson &amp; Johnson,

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.770
which produces a single-dose vaccine,

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:12.930
all said they were developing
Omicron-specific vaccines,

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:15.820
but those updates could
take months to be produced.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.250
For now, drug makers

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.620
are approaching additional
doses differently.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.420
Pfizer CEO, Albert Bourla,
said, "A fourth dose

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.150
is not necessarily needed."

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.650
Well, Moderna advised that
those who have had three doses

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:29.543
of its vaccine, may need
a second booster by fall.

00:03:29.543 --> 00:03:30.870
(slow music)

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:33.050
For these researchers,
it will also take time

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:35.190
to draw our conclusions
that can answer questions

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:39.140
such as, how long protection
from extra boosters can last.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:41.130
But like many other
experts around the world,

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:43.310
Regev-Yochay already says four shots

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:45.180
shouldn't be given out to everyone.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.290
- I would I think that probably we need

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:51.320
to save these vaccines
only to really the people

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.080
who are very vulnerable and needed,

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.825
and not give it out to
the whole population.

00:03:55.825 --> 00:03:57.130
- [Narrator] In other words,

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.870
people who are
immunocompromised, for example,

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:02.440
are more exposed to the risk
of getting seriously ill,

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:05.600
even after vaccination, but
for healthy individuals,

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:06.970
some scientists argue two

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:09.650
or three shots already
offer enough protection

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:10.850
for the worst symptoms.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.000
That argument comes as research suggests

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.070
the Omicron variant may
cause milder infection.

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:18.300
Hospitalizations associated with Omicron

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:21.600
in the US are lower compared
to prior variants, though,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.350
it could be too soon to
make definitive conclusions.

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:27.180
(slow music)

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.930
The number of daily coronavirus
cases reached new highs

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.170
this winter, in countries with high rates

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:34.690
of vaccination are taking
different approaches

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:36.070
to second boosters.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:37.690
Some are racing ahead.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:40.360
Israel has offered them to at-risk groups.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:44.527
(Naftali speaks foreign language)

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.700
Well, Chile and Brazil are also moving

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.700
to provide additional doses,
after initial campaigns

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:53.070
use less effective Chinese-made vaccines.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:57.487
(Sebastian speaks foreign language)

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:02.900
But government experts in the UK

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.400
said a second booster
shot isn't a priority,

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.740
and EU regulators said

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.260
frequent shots could
weaken the immune system.

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:10.170
- It's not something

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:13.650
that we can think should
be repeated constantly.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:15.970
- [Narrator] While the world
health organization cautioned,

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:18.240
blanket booster programs could, in fact,

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:19.540
prolong the pandemic.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.780
- By diverting supply to countries

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:25.193
that already have high levels
of vaccination coverage,

00:05:25.193 --> 00:05:30.024
giving the virus more
opportunity to spread and mutate.

00:05:30.024 --> 00:05:30.857
(background chatter)

00:05:30.857 --> 00:05:32.430
- [Narrator] For now in Tel Aviv,

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:36.260
researchers also recommend
taking more time for reflection.

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:39.020
- I hope that it's not going
to be a policy of giving it

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:42.400
to everybody, at least not
yet when we don't have data.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.470
If we will learn that that's
really what's necessary,

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:48.473
it might change the story, but
I'm not convinced about that.

